.TITLE "networksetup"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Configures network settings and services. It provides a command-line interface for managing __Wi-Fi__, __Ethernet__, and other network interfaces as well as __DNS__ and __proxy__ settings.

.DIV "TLDR"
**networksetup -listallnetworkservices**
Lists all network services configured on the system.
> __-listallnetworkservices__ list command

**networksetup -getinfo "Wi-Fi"**
Displays IP address, subnet mask, and other details for a specific service.
> __-getinfo__ info flag | __"Wi-Fi"__ service name

**networksetup -setdnsservers "Wi-Fi" 8.8.8.8**
Configures a specific DNS server for a network service.
> __-setdnsservers__ DNS config flag | __"Wi-Fi"__ service name | __8.8.8.8__ DNS address

**networksetup -setairportpower en0 on**
Turns the Wi-Fi power on or off for a specific hardware interface.
> __-setairportpower__ power flag | __en0__ interface identifier | __on__ state

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __networksetup__ is often more reliable than the GUI for fixing persistent connectivity issues. Most configuration changes require __administrator__ privileges.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
